<section class="shell band">
  <h2>Mindful trail retreats</h2>
  <div class="split">
    <div>
      <p>An annual retreat for interns, associates and licensed therapists. We walk, and the
      subject is presence: what it feels like when you have it, what takes it away, and what
      you do instead when you have lost it.</p>
      <p>It is not a conference and there is no curriculum to get through. Expect quiet,
      movement, small-group work, and more silence than most professional events are
      comfortable with.</p>
      <p>Associates in supervision with Reem are included in the annual retreat. Others are
      welcome as space allows.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Good fit if</h3>
      <ul class="plain">
        <li>You give your clients regulation skills you do not practice yourself.</li>
        <li>You are competent and quietly exhausted.</li>
        <li>You want professional development that is not another slide deck.</li>
        <li>You are curious about somatic work but have only read about it.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band--sand">
  <div class="shell">
    <h2>Working with horses</h2>
    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <p>Horses respond to what your nervous system is doing, not to what you intend or say.
        A therapist who is subtly braced gets a different horse than one who is settled, and the
        feedback arrives in seconds rather than in a supervision session three weeks later.</p>
        <p>Two ways in. Associates in supervision can add equine-assisted sessions at $60 each
        as part of their supervision. Licensed therapists who want to bring horses into their
        own practice can train with Reem, for a separate fee.</p>
        <p>Location is Dripping Springs, Texas. Sessions are scheduled individually, and a
        conversation comes first either way.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dl class="facts">
          <div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Dripping Springs, Texas</dd></div>
          <div><dt>For associates</dt><dd>$60 per session, optional, alongside supervision</dd></div>
